==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Only One Rarity}}

==Battleground==
*4 [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*3 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*5 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*1 [[Ragin' Gory]] spawns after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[J.K. Bun Bun]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Generally the easiest of this set of Otherworld Colosseum stages, it features exclusively Red and Dark enemies, most of which have less-than-stellar stats and serve more as life insurance policyholders than genuine threats. The only problematic enemies to watch out for are the Ragin' Gory, and J.K. Bun Bun respectively. However, both spawn individually from one another, which makes them exponentially easier to take care of. This stage simply serves as an introduction to the gimmick of the following stages: the Only One Rarity restriction.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
===='''Normal Cats'''====
*[[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]]: Having [[Strong Against|Strong VS]] Red enemies, they are capable of taking huge chunks off two problematic peons that this stage has. Island Cat fares very well against the boss of the stage too, being capable of landing a few good shots before taking to the bench. Their cooldown also allows them to be re-deployed almost immediately post-mortem, making them an excellent pick for a gimmicky stage like this.

===='''Special Cats'''====
*[[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Talented Heavy Assault C.A.T.]]: With their high speed, and exceedingly high damage against Dark enemies, they're a useful multi-purpose tool that can fill any role you need. C.A.T. can rush into enemy front lines to tank blows meant for more important units, deal high damage against annoying peons, and they will typically leave the field before overstaying their welcome. With a low recharge time, they will always be up and running whenever you need them.

===='''Rare Cats'''====
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Courier carries [[Massive Damage]] against Red enemies, with [[Behemoth Slayer]] to completely close the curtain on all but one of this colosseum's combatants. He completely outranges every threat in this stage, and can handle the boss with relative ease so long as you keep him safe. There is little contest to which Rare unit you want on the field at all times.

===='''Super Rare Cats'''====
*[[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]]: They are [[Resistant]] to Red enemies, with an off chance to [[Weaken]]. On their own, they are capable of stalling J.K. Bun Bun for extended periods of time, even longer if Weaken activates consistently. Pairing them up with Courier Cat can create a wall of hurt for every enemy in this stage; it is almost impenetrable to everything besides the Doge Darks which can and will inevitably push their way through despite your best efforts. Regardless, Roe Cat is an excellent pick for this stage.

